      "senderName": "NWS Tallahassee FL",
      "headline": "Special Marine Warning issued October 10 at 12:47PM EDT until October 10 at 2:45PM EDT by NWS Tallahassee FL",
      "description": "SMWTAE\n\nThe National Weather Service in Tallahassee has issued a\n\n* Special Marine Warning for...\nApalachee Bay or Coastal Waters From Keaton Beach to Ochlockonee\nRiver Fl out to 20 Nm...\nCoastal waters from  Suwannee River to Keaton Beach out 20 NM...\nWaters from Suwannee River to Apalachicola FL from 20 to 60 NM...\n\n* Until 245 PM EDT.\n\n* At 1247 PM EDT, severe thunderstorms capable of producing\nwaterspouts were located along a line extending from 10 nm\nnortheast of Buckeye Reef to 22 nm south of V Tower, moving\nnortheast at 25 knots.\n\nHAZARD...Waterspouts and wind gusts 34 knots or greater.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Waterspouts can quickly form and capsize boats...damage\nvessels...and create suddenly higher waves. Make sure all\non board are in a secure location and wearing life\njackets. Expect wind gusts in excess of 34\nknots...suddenly higher waves...frequent lightning...and\nheavy downpours. Make sure all on board are wearing life\njackets.\n\n* Locations impacted include...\nBuckeye Reef.",
      "instruction": "Move to safe harbor until hazardous weather passes.\n\nThunderstorms can produce sudden waterspouts. Waterspouts can easily\noverturn boats and create locally hazardous seas. Seek safe harbor\nimmediately.",
      "response": "Avoid",
